## Case text

Title, from ck.db `zephyr_cases` key `AWPTCM-T44301`:
**"(281) Management_Trap - Per-port link trap"**. Folder
`/New Platform Test (MASTER)/New Platform Template/Management`, labels
`["New_Platform_Management"]`, script_type STEP_BY_STEP, status Draft.

🔴 **THERE IS NO AUTHORED STEP TEXT.** `num_steps 1`, `has_objective 0`, single step
`[{"description":"","testData":"","expected":""}]` -- all three fields empty. Confirmed from
ck.db with `tools/tb tool tb277 cksnmpmon ckcase AWPTCM-T44301`, and stated in the dispatch.
**No objective, no precondition, no step description, no test data and no expected result exist
to quote.** Every step below was designed by the tester from the title, from the DUT's own CLI
surface (enumerated read-only in T44308 STEP 2 before anything in this group was configured),
and from RFC 3418, which defines the linkDown and linkUp notifications the title names.

The word the whole case turns on is **per-port**. So the design is a matched pair: two ports of
the same model, on the same DUT, cabled to the same partner switch, flapped the same way in the
same capture window -- one with the per-port trap armed and one without. A trap for the armed
port and silence for the other is the only evidence that actually says "per-port".

