## STEP 8 -- reboot persistence: NOT MEASURED

🔴 This case performed no reload and wrote nothing to startup-config, so **persistence of
`snmp trap link-status` across a reboot is NOT MEASURED and is not claimed.** The reason is the
group's, not this case's: the L3 underlay (vlan10 on port1.0.10, vlan48 on port1.0.48) exists in
running-config only -- the boot config is `flash:/default.cfg` -- so a reload destroys the path
to the trap receiver, and writing it to startup-config is a change to the standing bench
(STANDING-ORDERS §4), never taken unattended. Already in the queue as a NEEDS TEST ENGINEER item
from group A; nothing new is asked.

