## Verdict

The case is about one word, per-port, and that word was measured rather than inferred. With the
global `nsm` trap group armed and no per-port configuration, a full flap of port1.0.2 produced
nothing. With `snmp trap link-status` on port1.0.2 alone, the same flap produced a linkDown and
a linkUp on the wire, each naming ifIndex 5002 -- measured, not assumed, from
`ifDescr.5002 = port1.0.2` -- and each carrying the correct ifAdminStatus and ifOperStatus for
its direction. In the same capture window, the identical flap of port1.0.16, a sibling port to
the same partner switch, produced nothing, while the DUT's own log shows it detected and
recorded all four transitions in identical words. Removing the one per-port line returned the
behaviour to silence under the identical stimulus. The bench ended in its starting state, RSTP
roles included.

Reboot persistence is **NOT MEASURED** for the bench reason in STEP 8, and that limb is not
claimed anywhere above.

